  "subdivision_of_building": "First and second floor flat (52a Broad Street). Proposals relate specifically to the replacement of existing front elevation windows",
  "status": "Application Under Consideration",
  "description": "Proposal: Replacement of existing single-glazed timber sash windows with like-for-like double-glazed timber sash windows.\n\nDescription of Development: Replacement of existing single-glazed timber sash windows to the front elevations on first and second floor with new double-glazed timber sash windows (with acoustic glass) matching the original opening method, design, proportions and detailing of the existing windows.\n\nSite Description: The application property, 52A Broad Street, Teddington, is a two-storey residential maisonette located above a ground-floor commercial unit. The building forms part of a continuous terrace within Broad Street and lies within the Broad Street Conservation Area. The property features traditional timber sash windows consistent with the prevailing character of the surrounding Victorian/Edwardian streetscape.\n\nHeritage & Conservation Statement: The property is located within the Broad Street Conservation Area, where preserving the character and appearance of the area is a key planning consideration.The proposed works have been carefully designed to preserve and enhance the building’s contribution to the conservation area by:\n    •    Retaining the traditional timber sash window form\n    •    Matching original detailing and proportions\n    •    Avoiding the use of non-traditional materials such as uPVC\n\nThe introduction of slimline double glazing will not result in any significant visual harm, as the units are designed to replicate the appearance of traditional single glazing.The proposal therefore preserves the character and appearance of the conservation area in accordance with local and national planning policy.\n\nJustification / Planning Statement: The proposed replacement windows will significantly improve the thermal efficiency and acoustic performance of the property, contributing to improved residential amenity and energy efficiency. considerations with modern performance standards.\n",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Please provide either drawings to scale which includes scale bar or provide good quality detailed photos of existing (with annotation) please also provide manufacturers specs.\r\n\r\nIf you can please confirm whether window installer is FENSA Certified? if not then please provide Reasonable Exception Statement (RES) required for Fire Safety Strategy"
